,title,link,text,language,family
0,Languages of Africa - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Languages_of_Africa,The Niger–Congo languages constitute the largest language family spoken in West Africa and perhaps the world in terms of the number of languages. [citation needed] One of its salient features is an elaborate noun class system with grammatical concord.,"Swahili, Congo",Niger-Congo
1,Niger-Congo languages - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL67dm6qliEMCSwzycHfZuedyqui7wHIOz,Niger-Congo languages. 26 видео 32 485 просмотров Обновлен 20 мая 2026 г. Сохранить плейлист.,"Swahili, Congo",Niger-Congo
2,"Swahili, Congo | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/swc/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..jar6qQ3fv0gTuGqK6dNj_V4DtNH5tlO1FjqYOk2szWc,Congo Swahili is a language of wider communication that originated in the Democratic Republic of the Congo. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family and is part of the Swahili macrolanguage. Direct evidence is lacking...,"Swahili, Congo",Niger-Congo
3,"Swahili language | African Lingua Franca, Bantu Language | Britannica",https://www.britannica.com/topic/Swahili-language,"Swahili is a Bantu language spoken across the east coast of Africa. The Bantu languages form a subgroup of the Benue-Congo branch of the Niger-Congo language family. There are roughly 15 Swahili dialects, with the Kiunguja dialect serving as the base for standard Swahili.","Swahili, Congo",Niger-Congo
4,Swahili People in Congo | TikTok,https://www.tiktok.com/discover/swahili-people-in-congo,"Congo Swahili language culture, Congolese Swahili traditions, Swahili people in Congo, the influence of Swahili in Congo, Congolese Swahili communities Last updated 2026-06-08.Fragmento de mi columna musical en @republicaz @estamosenunarz .","Swahili, Congo",Niger-Congo
5,Niger-Congo Languages (Doctorate Africa),https://www.hauniversity.org/en/Niger-Congo-Languages.shtml,"The most spoken Niger-Congo languages according to the number of native speakers are Swahili, Yoruba, Igbo, Fula and Shona. The traditional branches and main languages of the Nigerian-Congolese family are: Kordofanian languages: spoken in Southern Sudan.","Swahili, Congo",Niger-Congo
6,Learn NIGER CONGO SWAHILI ZULU - Mind Luster,https://www.mindluster.com/lesson/300574-video,"Niger-Congo Languages Course: Embark on a captivating linguistic journey through the vast and diverse Niger-Congo language family. Explore languages like Swahili, Yoruba, Zulu, and Wolof. Delve into grammar, vocabulary, and cultural nuances.","Swahili, Congo",Niger-Congo
7,Top 10 Most Spoken Languages in Africa (2026) - VerboLabs,https://www.verbolabs.com/most-spoken-languages-in-africa/,"Regions Found. Niger-Congo. Swahili, Yoruba, Igbo, Zulu. West, Central, Southern Africa.Nigeria: Over 500 languages. Democratic Republic of Congo: Around 215. South Africa: 11 official languages. This makes Africa the most linguistically diverse continent in the world.","Swahili, Congo",Niger-Congo
8,African languages: The top 70 most spoken languages in Africa,https://www.berlitz.com/blog/what-are-most-spoken-languages-africa,"Igbo is one of Nigeria's major languages, spoken primarily in the southeastern region. It belongs to the Niger-Congo family and features a rich oral tradition, including folktales, proverbs, and songs.","Swahili, Congo",Niger-Congo
9,Languages of Africa - TopLangs.com,https://toplangs.com/languages-of-africa/,"Niger-Congo covers a huge share of sub-Saharan Africa and includes the Bantu branch as well as many non-Bantu branches. If a reader wants the single broad family with the widest footprint in Africa, this is the place to start.","Swahili, Congo",Niger-Congo
